From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] update_engine: refuse OTA downgrades on user builds again

Evolution X's 59fbd47 also makes HardwareAndroid::AllowDowngrade()
return true, so update_engine applies a payload older than the running
build (ErrorCode::kPayloadTimestampError is never returned). Put back
LineageOS's check (9b4309a): a downgrade only with
ro.ota.allow_downgrade=true on a build that isn't a user build. On
ExpressiveOS's user builds that means never.
---
 aosp/hardware_android.cc |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aosp/hardware_android.cc b/aosp/hardware_android.cc
index 9bef40dd..61b23886 100644
--- a/aosp/hardware_android.cc
+++ b/aosp/hardware_android.cc
@@ -265,7 +265,8 @@ int64_t HardwareAndroid::GetBuildTimestamp() const {
 // Returns true if the device runs an userdebug build, and explicitly allows OTA
 // downgrade.
 bool HardwareAndroid::AllowDowngrade() const {
-  return true;
+  return GetBoolProperty("ro.ota.allow_downgrade", false) &&
+         GetProperty("ro.build.type", "") != "user";
 }
 
 bool HardwareAndroid::GetFirstActiveOmahaPingSent() const {
-- 
